/// =============================================================================
/// Model2 calculation groups
///
/// Calculation groups are the main reason this model exists. Without them,
/// every base measure needs a hand-written YTD, prior-year, and growth variant,
/// and the set has to be maintained by hand as measures are added. That is
/// where the classic "the numbers disagree between two pages" defect comes
/// from.
///
/// With a calculation group, [Total Sales] is defined once. The group supplies
/// the time variants at query time, so a new base measure automatically gains
/// YTD, PY, and growth without anyone writing them.
///
/// --- A caveat on this file ----------------------------------------------
///
/// The syntax below is written to be illustrative rather than authoritative.
/// Calculation groups are serialised differently across Power BI Desktop
/// versions, and the exact TMDL representation is version-dependent. Treat
/// this file as a design reference for *what* the groups should contain and
/// *why*, and export the real definition from your own model rather than
/// assuming this will load as-is. See README.md.
/// =============================================================================

/// =============================================================================
/// Time Intelligence
///
/// Selects the time variant applied to any numeric measure in scope.
///
/// SelectItemValue switches the measure as the user moves through the group,
/// so the slicer cycles Current -> YTD -> PY -> Growth. The selected item is
/// what changes the number, not which measure is displayed.
/// =============================================================================

calculationGroup 'Time Intelligence'
    formatStringDefinition: "$#,##0.00"

    calculationItem 'Current'
        formula:
            SELECTEDMEASURE()

    calculationItem 'YTD'
        formula:
            CALCULATE(
                SELECTEDMEASURE(),
                DATESYTD('DimDate'[Date])
            )

    calculationItem 'PY'
        formula:
            CALCULATE(
                SELECTEDMEASURE(),
                SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR('DimDate'[Date])
            )

    calculationItem 'Growth %'
        formula:
            VAR Current = SELECTEDMEASURE()
            VAR Prior = CALCULATE(SELECTEDMEASURE(), SAMEPERIODLASTYEAR('DimDate'[Date]))
            RETURN
                DIVIDE(Current - Prior, Prior)

    /// Precedence matters: a measure used on a fiscal slicer should not have a
    /// calendar YTD silently applied to it. Rows higher in this list are
    /// evaluated first, and the first one that returns a value wins.
    preemptionPriority: 1

/// =============================================================================
/// Currency Conversion
///
/// A second, orthogonal axis. Combining it with Time Intelligence means a
/// report can show current-currency YTD figures without any base measure
/// knowing about either concept.
///
/// This is the pattern that shows why calculation groups compose: Time
/// Intelligence and Currency Conversion are independent, and the model
/// supports all four combinations without a single duplicated measure.
/// =============================================================================

calculationGroup 'Currency'
    formatStringDefinition: "$#,##0.00"

    calculationItem 'Reporting Currency'
        formula:
            VAR Rate =
                CALCULATE(
                    MAX('DimCurrency'[Rate]),
                    'DimCurrency'[Currency Code] = SELECTEDVALUE('DimCurrency'[Currency Code], "USD")
                )
            VAR Amount = SELECTEDMEASURE()
            RETURN
                IF(ISBLANK(Rate), Amount, Amount * Rate)

    /// Left blank, the group does nothing, so a report with no currency slicer
    /// shows the base measure untouched.
    calculationItem 'Base'
        formula:
            SELECTEDMEASURE()

    preemptionPriority: 2

/// =============================================================================
/// Notes
/// =============================================================================
///
/// 1. A calculation group applies to every numeric measure in scope, including
///    measures on other fact tables. Scope it with a FormatStringDefinition
///    and, where a group must not touch a particular measure, exclude that
///    measure explicitly.
///
/// 2. SELECTEDMEASURE() returns the measure currently in context. A calculation
///    item that does not use it will return the same value regardless of which
///    measure is displayed, which is almost always a mistake.
///
/// 3. Time intelligence applied to a non-additive measure such as
///    [Closing Units On Hand] is meaningless. Calculation groups do not know
///    which measures are additive, so this must be handled by measure design:
///    keep non-additive measures in a separate display folder and do not put
///    them in scope for the group.
///
/// 4. Test calculation groups in Desktop with *View as > Calculation group* to
///    confirm each item behaves as intended before publishing.
///
/// 5. After adding a calculation group, re-check existing reports. A measure
///    that was already a measure can now be reached through the group, and
///    conditional formatting or field parameters that referenced it may need
///    updating.
